# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER COMMIT CITIZEN DATA
# Downloaded backups are real citizen documents (medical certificates,
# good-conduct certificates, payment receipts, board decisions).
# They live in D:\mocd-docfix-data, OUTSIDE this repo, by design.
# These patterns are a second line of defence in case that ever changes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
backup/
data/
downloads/
*.pdf
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.doc
*.docx
*.xls
*.xlsx

# Reports, manifests, state and logs contain document ids, file paths and
# citizen file names. Keep them out of the repo too.
reports/
state/
logs/
*.jsonl
scan-*.csv
migration-report-*.csv
review-*.csv
quarantine-*.csv
audit-*.log

# The ledger and its companions. repair-<env>.csv holds every document's name,
# path and CRM link; errors-<env>.txt holds whatever a failed call returned.
# Both live in D:\mocd-docfix-data by design — these patterns are the safety net.
repair-*.csv
errors-*.txt

# Secrets — API keys and CRM credentials are never stored in the repo.
#
# They live in %APPDATA%\mocd-docfix\, outside this tree, encrypted per Windows account, so
# nothing below should ever match. These patterns are the second line of defence for the day
# somebody drops a copy in here to "try something".
appsettings.*.json
!appsettings.Example.json
*.env
secrets.json
secrets.dat
config.json
credentials*.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .NET
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
bin/
obj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/
TestResults/
*.trx
*.coverage
coverage*.xml
coverage*.json
